    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners` so that when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, this generates a `LocalDate registrationDate` in both `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output). `format: date` makes Jackson serialize it as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping the DTO to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it is `null`. A supplied date is left untouched.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`db/h2`, `db/hsqldb`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. (The test harness uses HSQLDB.)\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed. This satisfies both scenarios: defaulting to today when absent, and preserving a supplied date (`2020-06-15`).",
